<article class="env-proposition" id="E1B237">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/E1B237">Proposition <span data-tag="E1B237">5.2.2.9</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ and $\calD $ be $\infty $-categories, and let $f: \calC \rightarrow \calD $ and $g: \calD \rightarrow \calC $ be adjoint functors. Then $f$ and $g$ induce adjoint functors $\rm {h} \it {f}: \rm {h} \it {\calC } \rightarrow \rm {h} \it {\calD }$ and $\rm {h} \it {g}:\rm {h} \it {\calD } \rightarrow \rm {h} \it {\calC }$ between ($\calH $-enriched) homotopy categories. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows immediately from Proposition <a href="/tag/71F6CA" data-tag="71F6CA">5.2.2.8</a>, since a unit transformation $\id _{\calC } \rightarrow g \circ f$ induces a unit transformation $\id _{\rm {h} \it {\calC }} \rightarrow (\rm {h} \it {g}) \circ (\rm {h} \it {f})$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>